---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = `${import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '')}/`;
---
<BaseLayout title="Projects" description="Real software projects behind Mika's self-taught developer roadmap.">
  <section>
    <p class="kicker">proof through building</p>
    <h2>Projects</h2>
    <p>The projects are not side quests from the roadmap. They are where the roadmap comes from. Each one exposes a different set of gaps, forces concepts to become practical, and leaves behind lessons that turn into field notes.</p>
    <ul class="project-list">
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/miflow13/mochi-desktop">Mochi 🌱</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">python · gtk4 · cairo · linux desktop · stateful systems</p>
        <p>A handcrafted Linux desktop companion. Mochi has been a laboratory for application lifecycle, state machines, rendering, animation, packaging, testing, platform behavior, and turning a growing app into reusable architecture.</p>
        <p><a href="https://miflow13.github.io/mochi-desktop/">website →</a> · <a href={`${base}topics/`}>related field notes →</a></p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/miflow13/Oniria">Oniria</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">next.js · react three fiber · three.js · sanity · spatial ux</p>
        <p>A walkable 3D library built around live content. It has taught me about spatial interfaces, CMS-backed systems, performance, interaction state, debugging 3D environments, and shipping an ambitious prototype under a deadline.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/miflow13/ravel">Ravel</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">typescript · agents · containers · evaluation · security boundaries</p>
        <p>An agent-behavior evaluation project focused on the difference between what an agent claims it did and what the environment can actually observe.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3><a href="https://github.com/miflow13/KeyFlip">KeyFlip</a></h3>
        <p class="meta">linux utility · input devices · desktop integration</p>
        <p>A small Linux utility for quickly toggling a laptop's internal keyboard while leaving external keyboards alone. Small enough to understand end to end, but real enough to expose packaging and platform constraints.</p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
